hi I'm Annie whoo and I'm a mathematics  teacher I think it's a really common  struggle that many people students and  adults alike have experienced that they  maybe were encounter encounter a problem  and they couldn't arrive at that final  number or the final number they arrived  that wasn't the one that the teacher was  searching for and for me I think that's  that that experience there of not being  able to get there it sort of really  takes the wind out of someone's  mathematical reasoning and thinking and  self-concept because how do they end  that experience they just end up feeling  like a failure I think back to you know  the lessons of storytelling and you can  have you could have a movie or a play or  a book that has a kind of the average  beginning and okay middle and it has a  great ending then you come out of it  thinking that was amazing and conversely  it's true you can start off with a great  punch and have a very amazing surprising  middle but if you end in a way that is  dissatisfying  and sort of leaves you deflated you go  away from that experience very much  disliking it and that's there's an  emotional sort of resonance there I  would like that was not was not a great  experience and many people feel  mathematics that way they forget about  the journey that they took to understand  ah what what all these pieces how did  they all fit together and then I made  some routine arithmetic error that meant  my number at the end was 10 times larger  than it was supposed to be and just  because my decimal point was in the  wrong spot I feel like all the things  that I went through before were  meaningless and so I think that emphasis  on the end point is dangerous in that  way at the end point is not you know  worthless it's really it's one of the  most powerful things about mathematics  that it can solve problems that you  might think are insurmountable but  through the application of logic and  reasoning we can get there but if we  emphasize that at the expense of all of  these other things all the reasoning and  thinking and collaboration and talking  and dialogue to arrive at that point I  think we saw our students a false bill  of goods about what mathematics is  [Music]
 

